Your First Shell Script
Let’s walk through a basic example to see how shell scripting works.

Step 1: Create the Script
Open your terminal and create a new file 
    vim hello.sh
Add the following lines:
    pwd
    ls
    date

Step 2: Give Execute Permission
By default, the script doesn't have permission to run. Use chmod to give it execute rights:
  chmod +x first.sh

Step 3: Run the Script
Execute the script using:
  ./first.sh

Expected Output
    /home/tom/shell_scripting
    echo.sh  hello.sh
    Tue Apr 8 21:34:31 IST 2025

________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________________

Explaining the Commands
pwd – Shows the current working directory.
date – Displays the current date and time.
chmod +x – Grants execute permission to the script.
./first.sh – Runs the script from the current directory.



